<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">The problem</div>
      <h2>Creating a strategy was never the hard part.</h2>
      <p>Most engagements produce an inspirational deck, a six-figure invoice, and a mission that quietly stalls anyway. Three months later the energy the team invested is gone, and so is the appetite to try again. We believe 95% of the value of any strategy lies in its delivery &mdash; so that&rsquo;s where we spend our time, and where the mission actually gets carried across the finish line.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div><div class="stat-num">12&ndash;18</div><div class="stat-label">months to carry a critical mission through to a delivered result</div></div>
      <div><div class="stat-num">$35M&rarr;$2B+</div><div class="stat-label">revenue range of organizations whose missions we&rsquo;ve delivered</div></div>
      <div><div class="stat-num">25+</div><div class="stat-label">years applying this method across industries</div></div>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="pull-quote">&ldquo;We almost go as far as saying that strategy is not the complicated part. It&rsquo;s the act of delivering it that decides whether it was worth doing at all.&rdquo;</blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

